+ * A front's tween on the hand's clock (T9-M20 D10, the displacement clause): one pencil-boil
+ * `sequence` carries the rAF timeline and the tween's own clock advances by at most one of the
+ * panel's frames per tick (`MOTION.hand.stepMs` at 60 Hz and above, the observed frame below),
+ * so a frame the main thread lost pauses the front for one frame's travel instead of landing it
+ * wherever the wall clock says. A healthy frame at any refresh rate is never slowed.
+ * `onComplete` fires when the tween's clock, not the wall's, reaches `durationMs`. Under reduced
+ * motion the sequence never starts: the consumer lands its value itself, as before.
